      "topic_id": "indices_common_base_equations",
      "prompt": "Solve 81^(x+3) = 27^(2x).",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Write both sides as powers of 3: 81 = 3^4 and 27 = 3^3",
        "81^(x+3) = 27^(2x) becomes 3^(4(x+3)) = 3^(3×2x), i.e. 3^(4x+12) = 3^(6x)",
        "Since the bases match, the powers must be equal: 4x + 12 = 6x",
        "Rearranging: -2x = -12, so x = -12/-2 = 6"
      ],
      "final_answer": "6",
      "marks": 5,
      "mark_scheme": [
        {
          "code": "M1",
          "description": "Write both sides as powers of 3: 81 = 3^4 and 27 = 3^3",
          "marks": 1
